# False error: CSmPlayer.GetCurrentEntityID — Openplanet-injected method missing from typedb

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

Found 2026-08-30 while checking tm-dips-plus-plus. The game compiles this; the LSP does not. Same family as GH #21 (`MwAddRef`/`MwRelease`): Openplanet injects methods the Nadeo dump never lists.

## Steps to Reproduce

1. Check any plugin that calls `player.GetCurrentEntityID()` on a `CSmPlayer@` (tm-dips-plus-plus, tm-change-car-color, tm-magic-spectator), or the one-file repro below.
2. `openplanet-lsp check` reports an error on the call.

Minimal:

```angelscript
void Use(CSmPlayer@ player) {
    auto entId = player.GetCurrentEntityID();
}
```

## Expected Behavior

Silent. Openplanet injects `uint GetCurrentEntityID()` on `CGamePlayer` (no args). It returns an offset value. `CSmPlayer` inherits `CGamePlayer`, so the call is legal and the in-game compiler accepts it.

## Actual Behavior

```
src/PlayerState.as:121:22: error
type `ShootMania::CSmPlayer` has no member `GetCurrentEntityID`
```

tm-dips-plus-plus currently has to whitelist that exact substring in `tools/lsp-known-errors.txt` so its LSP gate stays live for real errors.

## Why

Typedb (`OpenplanetNext.json`, both the live dump and `tests/fixtures/typedb/`):

- `ShootMania::CSmPlayer` parent `CGamePlayer`
- `Game::CGamePlayer` parent `CMwNod`, members: `User` only
- Neither type lists `GetCurrentEntityID`. `Openplanet.h` does not declare it either.

B006 trusts a Nadeo type's member list when it is non-empty, so this fires `UndefinedMember` instead of staying silent. The GH #21 special-case in `lookup_member` only covers `MwAddRef`/`MwRelease` on `CMwNod`-derived types.

The previous vscode-openplanet-angelscript already patched this at dump-convert time (`language-server/src/convert_nadeo.ts`):

```
if (ret.name == "CGamePlayer") {
    addToMethods({name: "GetCurrentEntityID", returntypedecl: "uint", args: [], isEnum: false, i: -1});
}
```

openplanet-lsp loads the dump as-is and has no equivalent injection.

## Live call sites (game accepts)

- tm-dips-plus-plus `src/PlayerState.as:121`
- tm-change-car-color `src/Main.as:72`
- tm-magic-spectator `src/PlayerState.as:105`

## Sibling injection (same class of bug — cover in this ticket)

`CGameCtnNetwork::GetManialinkPages()` is the other Openplanet-injected method in that convert script (`CGameManialinkPage@[]&`, no args). Also absent from the dump. tm-shadowless-chrono calls it. Same fix, not a second ticket.

(`MwAddRef`/`MwRelease` on `CMwNod` is the third injection in that script and is already GH #21.)

## Work

Mirror GH #21: treat Openplanet-injected methods as builtins, not dump members.

- `GetCurrentEntityID` on `CGamePlayer` and descendants → `uint`, no args
- `GetManialinkPages` on `CGameCtnNetwork` and descendants → `CGameManialinkPage@[]&`, no args

Prefer a small injected-methods table over two more hard-coded name matches, so the next Openplanet-only method is one row. Do not widen B006's "untrusted empty list" silence — `CSmPlayer`'s list is trusted and should stay trusted for real missing members.

Return type matters: a silent `Error("")` sentinel (what GH #21 does for void `MwAddRef`) would hide the call but type `auto entId` wrong. The method returns `uint`.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)

Red: `CSmPlayer@ p; auto id = p.GetCurrentEntityID();` currently `UndefinedMember`.

Variants:

- `CGamePlayer@` (the type it is actually declared on)
- `CSmPlayer@` (the live call-site type)
- wrong arity still errors
- wrong receiver (`CMwNod@ n; n.GetCurrentEntityID()`) still errors
- `GetManialinkPages` on `CGameCtnNetwork@`
- GH #21 `MwAddRef` stays silent

Game probe the fixture before treating the LSP silence as ground truth. A game ACCEPT on this machine can leak from other installed plugins; a game REJECT is solid.

## Related

GH #21 (`MwAddRef`/`MwRelease`), B006 (trusted Nadeo member lists), tm-dips-plus-plus `tools/lsp-known-errors.txt`.